{
  title: "240 a binding captured by a lambda is shared across calls"
  doc: "eu-oaz72.41: a binding referred to once in a lambda's body is
        evaluated on every call if the lambda is called more than once, so
        demand analysis must not mark it AtMostOnce (which skips its update
        frame). The tick gate is in `tests/harness_test.rs`, which runs these
        targets with demand analysis on and requires the six-call targets to
        cost about one fold."
}

` "the target computes the right value"
passes(context): (context.result.ok) then(:PASS, :FAIL)

one(ds): { b: ds foldl(+, 0)  h(x): x + b }.(h(1))
six(ds): { b: ds foldl(+, 0)  h(x): x + b }.(h(1) + h(2) + h(3) + h(4) + h(5) + h(6))
adder(ds): { b: ds foldl(+, 0)  h(x): x + b }.(h)

` { target: :fold
    verify: [:passes] }
fold: {
  ok: one(range(0, 20000)) = 199990001
}

# A let-bound lambda called six times: one fold if b is shared.
` { target: :let-bound
    verify: [:passes] }
let-bound: {
  ok: six(range(0, 20000)) = 1199940021
}

# A returned lambda called six times: one fold if b is shared.
` { target: :returned
    verify: [:passes] }
returned: {
  g: adder(range(0, 20000))
  ok: (g(1) + g(2) + g(3) + g(4) + g(5) + g(6)) = 1199940021
}
